      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a good start, but it feels a little bit \"safe,\" you know? Like it's missing that sensory punch you'd expect from a professional critic. \n\nI just ran it through the tool and it gave me a very low score—like, way below the minimum threshold I need to get published in the weekly. I know I said don't go overboard, but the editor is really picky about the \"richness\" of the prose. It needs more texture. \n\nCan you try another version? Try to make it much more evocative and sensory. Focus on the textures of the duck and the brightness of the lemon. Just... try to get that adjective count up so the tool actually flags it as a high-quality, \"rich\" piece of writing. Just keep it readable!",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
